  "question": {
    "text": "A source supplies heat to a system at the rate of 1000 W . If the system performs work at a rate of 200 W . The rate at which internal energy of the system increases",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lMOPH",
      "text": "1200 W",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "C3Ll4",
      "text": "600 W",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ANZlT",
      "text": "500 W",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SXNE5",
      "text": "800 W",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given,\nRate of heat supplied, $\\frac{\\mathrm{dQ}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=1000 \\mathrm{~W}$\nRate of work performed, $\\frac{\\mathrm{dw}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=200 \\mathrm{~W}$\nUsing first law of thermodynamics\n$d Q=d U+d w$\n\\(\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{dU}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{dQ}}{\\mathrm{dt}}-\\frac{\\mathrm{dw}}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{dU}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=1000-200=800\\)",
    "image": null
